AI Chatbot for IAM – Project Scope Document (v0.1)
1. Context & Project Objectives
The project aims to develop an intelligent AI Chatbot dedicated to MyIAM. It will assist users with their daily IAM inquiries, reduce the workload of support teams, and significantly enhance the user experience.

Phase 1 Objectives (Support Foundation):
Automate responses to Frequently Asked Questions (IAM FAQ).

Guide users through MyIAM procedures and processes (step-by-step).

Reduce ticket volume on ServiceNow and the influx of queries to the L1/L2 shared mailbox.

Knowledge Management: Centralize and structure IAM expertise, standardize information delivery, and ensure that any procedural changes are immediately and consistently communicated to all users.

Future Phase Objectives (Governance & Advanced AI) – To be confirmed:
Translate IAM business rules and clarify system decisions: Convert technical logs into plain language to eliminate misunderstandings and reduce support claims. Specifically:

Explain root causes for access rejections/revocations (SOD conflicts, approval timeouts, HR movements, etc.).

Clarify access lifecycles (recertification processes, request status/approval paths, birthrights, etc.).

Optimize request quality and compliance: Reduce invalid requests and entry errors by steering users toward the correct access based on their business needs.

Goal: Guarantee the Least Privilege principle + increase operational efficiency + improve data quality entering MyIAM.

Proactive SOD Conflict Prevention: Reduce SOD access requests upstream by guiding users toward compliant access during the advisory phase.

Business Role (BR) Management Assistance:

Analyze user profiles to recommend the most compliant Business Roles for their team/job function.

Assist Managers/Resource Owners/Role Owners in creating new BRs.

Data-Driven Insights: Analyze interactions to generate strategic KPIs for IAM steering:

Identify pain points (resources or processes generating the most questions/errors).

Identify knowledge gaps where the Chatbot could not provide an answer.

2. Target Users
2.1 User Scope
The Chatbot will be deployed for all MyIAM users.

2.2 User Personas
End users: Raise/track access requests, view workitems, self-certification.

Line managers: Team access requests, manage Business Roles, manage team FRC, line manager certification.

Role owners: Manage business roles, role membership certification.

Resource owners: Manage applications/entitlements, resource owner certification.

Support teams & Admins: All of the above, plus workgroup management.

3. Primary Use Cases (v0.1)
FAQ Responses: (e.g., "What is the status of my request?", "How do I raise a 'Remove' request?", "How do I set up a delegation?")

Recertification Support: Answering questions related to ongoing campaigns.

Workflow Guidance: Explaining MyIAM concepts (SOD, App Profile, etc.) to prevent errors during entry.

4. Chatbot Features (v0.1)
Security & Compliance
Access Control & Eligibility: Data access restricted by user profile (e.g., standard users only see their own data).

Data Privacy: Filtering sensitive data and ensuring the Chatbot operates strictly within the secure MyIAM infrastructure (no external LLM transfers).

Audit Trail: Secure archiving of conversations for audit purposes.

Intelligent Response Engine (NLU & RAG)
Natural Language Understanding (NLU): Interpreting intent regardless of user jargon.

RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation): Extracting sourced, up-to-date information from official documentation (manuals, FAQs).

Connectivity & Tracking
Real-time Status Query: Secure connection to MyIAM to retrieve request progress via Request ID.

Blocker Identification: Identifying the current approver or team holding a ticket.

User Experience
Contextualization: Maintaining conversation history to avoid repetition.

Feedback Loop: "Helpful/Not helpful" buttons to identify documentary gaps.

